CLASS net/minecraft/unmapped/C_vhpmxtfv net/minecraft/block/MapColor
	COMMENT Represents the surface color of a block when rendered from the
	COMMENT {@linkplain net.minecraft.client.MinecraftClient#getMapRenderer() map renderer}.
	COMMENT Color names refer to a material or an object which refers to their vanilla
	COMMENT Minecraft textures, not their real-world counterparts, eg. "emerald green".
	COMMENT Names are in the form of either <i>blockReference_baseColor</i> or <i>color</i>.
	COMMENT <p>
	COMMENT When the map is rendered, the {@link MapColor.Brightness#brightness} value is
	COMMENT added to the base color. This "rendered color" can be obtained with
	COMMENT {@link MapColor#getRenderColor(MapColor.Brightness)},
	COMMENT and is represented in RGBA.
